-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attribution: upstream framework
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DUIN is built on Lamprey-Harness (published as "lamprey" when DUIN forked it on
2026-05-30):

  Lamprey-Harness
  https://github.com/USS-Parks/Lamprey-Harness
  Copyright (c) 2026 Basho Parks
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  (The notice at the fork point read "Copyright (c) 2026 Lamprey Contributors";
  LICENSE retains both forms.)

Lamprey-Harness provides the desktop agent shell, chat UX, skills/MCP
integration, and the Electron + React build pipeline. DUIN builds on it as a
second-brain agent for non-coders: a pluggable agent/brain connector (AG-UI), an
animated 2D/3D causal-graph brain with foresight engines (propagation,
predicted-risks, world-state, insights, decision-loop, calibration), notes
extraction, and a first-run interview.

Legacy identifiers. A few on-disk, environment and settings names still carry
the upstream name. They are kept on purpose: renaming them needs a migration of
existing installs, which is out of scope for this release.

  lamprey.db, lamprey-YYYY-MM-DD.db     the SQLite database and its backups
  lamprey-memory/                       the memory store directory
  LAMPREY_HOOK_*                        environment passed to hook scripts
  LAMPREY_BUILD_*, LAMPREY_GITHUB_*     build-time defines (electron.vite.config.ts)
  lamprey-agent/<...>                   git branch prefix of executor worktrees
  lamprey://                            deep-link scheme, handled alongside duin://
  lamprey-mint                          a theme preset id (its label is "Mint")
  lamprey-git-tools, lamprey-research-helpers
                                        bundled plugin ids (userData/plugins/<id>)
  --lamprey-headless                    CLI flag, kept as an alias of --duin-headless

