-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled models and language data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None of these files are committed to the repository; a release build stages them
into resources/ (see resources/ocr/README.md, resources/ocr/models/README.md and
scripts/prepare-bundled-models.mjs). When absent, each feature degrades or
fetches on demand.

  PP-OCR models and dictionary  -  PaddlePaddle / PaddleOCR authors, Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR
  ONNX exports of the PP-OCR mobile detection / recognition (/ optional
  orientation) models plus the character dictionary, from
  huggingface.co/monkt/paddleocr-onnx or RapidAI/RapidOCR. Loaded by the
  flag-gated Tier-2 OCR engine (DUIN_OCR_ENGINE=paddle). The shipped dictionary
  is PaddleOCR's ppocr_keys_v1.txt (the PP-OCRv4 dictionary); which PP-OCR
  generation the ONNX files are is not asserted here.

  Tesseract language data  -  tessdata_fast, Apache-2.0
  https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_fast  (eng, chi_sim, jpn)
  Loaded by tesseract.js (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js)
  for the flag-gated Tier-1 OCR (DUIN_OCR=1).

  Xenova/multilingual-e5-small  -  MIT
  https://huggingface.co/Xenova/multilingual-e5-small
  ONNX (q8) conversion by Xenova of intfloat/multilingual-e5-small
  ("Multilingual E5 Text Embeddings", Wang et al.). The default embedder.

  Xenova/bge-reranker-base  -  MIT
  https://huggingface.co/Xenova/bge-reranker-base
  ONNX (q8) conversion by Xenova of BAAI/bge-reranker-base. The default reranker.

  Other encoders the app can use (bge-m3, nli-deberta-v3-small, ...) are not
  shipped; they are downloaded to the user's cache on first use.

