-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Concepts and techniques
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DUIN reimplements ideas from the following projects. No code was copied from
them; the credit is for the design.

  rtk (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk) and snip: the command-output
  filter concept behind DUIN's snip filters (electron/services/snip,
  resources/snip-filters) including the "rtk proxy"-style bypass and the len/4
  token estimate. DUIN's filters are re-authored with their own schema.

  Graphify (Apache-2.0 / MIT, https://github.com/safishamsi/graphify): the
  GRAPH_REPORT idea (community detection, hubs, cross-cluster bridges,
  EXTRACTED / INFERRED / AMBIGUOUS labelling) behind
  electron/services/brain/graph-insight.ts, written from scratch in TypeScript.

  deepseek-harness (MIT, DeepSeek, https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness):
  prefix-extension compaction (electron/services/model-compaction.ts), usage
  accounting (providers/usage-accounting.ts) and the Windows ACL sandbox
  approach (sandbox/win32.ts, resources/sandbox-win32/restrict-run.ps1),
  reimplemented in DUIN.

  OpenAI Codex: the apply_patch "Begin Patch / End Patch" envelope grammar
  (electron/services/apply-patch-tool.ts); DUIN's parser is hand-written.

  memtrace: the FactStatus honesty-contract discipline (an absent record is
  UNKNOWN, never a green light) used by electron/services/brain/operator-model.ts.
